A partial: the decisions-index steps the knowledge-workflow commands and the
dynamic commands share.

D-DECISIONS-LEARNING-GATE: a decisions load is gated on the settings line's
`CURATION`. Curation can be narrowed by the repository or the machine, and neither
can turn it back on (D-FEATURES-NARROW-ONLY). The settings line also reads
`CURATION=off` while git tracks the curation folders, or does not answer for them:
the files there are the repository's own content, and devflow reads nothing in a
folder it cannot tell is its own. So `decisions_gate()` is the one sentence every
decisions host carries: with `CURATION=off` the step is skipped before it locates a
ledger or reads an index. An unresolvable settings line reads `CURATION=off`, as the
fail-closed line does, because a failed resolution cannot show what git tracks. The
gate reads the line the host's settings block resolved above; this partial imports
nothing from `_settings.mds`. In a multi-worktree run the line is the start root's:
the root the ledger is located from.

D-LEARNING-VARIANTS: the gate guards a repository that narrows curation off on a machine
where it is on. On a machine with curation off the decisions text is absent altogether: the
whole of `decisions_load()` is a curation-on arm, so every expansion of it exists only in the
curation-on build. `decisions_gate()` and `decisions_locate()` are leaves, reached only from
inside an arm (`decisions_load()`, `authoring_decisions()`, or a host's own on arm), and carry
no arm of their own: an arm cannot nest.

D-DECISIONS-SLICE: the index is handed on as a slice, never whole. The orchestrating main model
copies the index lines that touch an agent's work, verbatim, behind a
`(slice: N of M entries — full index: <path>)` marker and ahead of the footer, so an agent reads what
bears on its task and `devflow:apply-decisions` sends it to the full index only when its work leaves
that scope. Siblings over one diff share ONE slice, so their prompts stay identical. No script cuts
it: the index stays a pre-rendered file read, never built on demand, and matching a line to a task is
judgment, which stays with the model. When unsure, include the line: a slice that misses costs one
full-index read, a slice that over-includes costs only its bytes. `decisions_slice()` is a leaf like
the gate and the locator, reached only from inside a curation-on arm, so a curation-off build carries
none of the rule (D-LEARNING-VARIANTS).

@define decisions_gate():
When the settings line says `CURATION=off`, set `DECISIONS_CONTEXT` to `(none)` and skip this step, locating no ledger and reading no index.
@end

@define decisions_locate():
The decisions ledger belongs to the repository, not to one checkout: a linked worktree reads the main worktree's copy, a subdirectory session the repository root's. Locate it with one git call, run from the start directory — `WORKTREE_PATH` if provided, otherwise cwd (`devflow:worktree-support`):

```bash
git -C "{start}" rev-parse --path-format=absolute --show-toplevel --git-common-dir
```

Line 1 is the checkout's toplevel, line 2 the common git directory. A git older than 2.31 echoes `--path-format=absolute` back as a line of its own first. `{ledger}` is the first that applies:

1. **The main worktree** — line 2 without its trailing `/.git`, when the output is exactly two lines each beginning with `/`, line 2 ends in `/.git`, and the directory left once it is removed is not your home directory and contains a `.devflow/` directory.
2. **The toplevel** — line 1, or on an older git the line after the echoed flag.
3. **The start directory itself** — when the command failed or printed no absolute toplevel (outside a git repository).

This is the rule the curation hooks apply, so you read the index the Curate agent writes.
@end

@define decisions_slice():
Hand each agent that takes `DECISIONS_CONTEXT` a slice, not the whole index: the index lines whose title, scope or area touch the files and task it works on, verbatim, led by `(slice: N of M entries — full index: <absolute index path>)` and closed by the index footer. When unsure, include the line. Siblings over one diff share ONE slice.
@end

@define decisions_load():
<!-- curation:on -->
### Load DECISIONS_CONTEXT

{{decisions_gate()}}

{{decisions_locate()}}

**Step 1 — Read the pre-rendered index** `{ledger}/.devflow/curation/index.md`. Its content is `DECISIONS_CONTEXT`; if it is absent or empty, `DECISIONS_CONTEXT` is `(none)`.

The index is one direct file read.

**Step 2 — Slice the index, then hand it on:**

When `DECISIONS_CONTEXT` is not `(none)`, hand it only to the agents whose contract declares it.

{{decisions_slice()}}

Those agents follow `devflow:apply-decisions`. A host that uses the index in its own thread says so in its own step.

<!-- curation:end -->
@end

@export decisions_gate
@export decisions_locate
@export decisions_slice
@export decisions_load
